                        <div class='deftext'>One of a pair of molecular entities which are mirror images of each other and non-<em><a href="/terms/view/S06144">superposable</a></em>.<div class='seealso' style='margin-top: 10px;'><b>See also:</b> <em><a href="/terms/view/E02079">enantiomorph</a></em></div><div class='sources' style='margin-top: 10px;'><b><em>Sources: </em></b><br/>PAC, 1994, <em>66</em>, 1077.  (<em>Glossary of terms used in physical organic chemistry (IUPAC Recommendations 1994)</em>) on page 1112 [<a href='/sources/view/0093'>Terms</a>]  [<a href='https://doi.org/10.1351/pac199466051077' target='_blank'>Paper</a>]<br/>PAC, 1996, <em>68</em>, 2193.  (<em>Basic terminology of stereochemistry (IUPAC Recommendations 1996)</em>) on page 2207 [<a href='/sources/view/0116'>Terms</a>]  [<a href='https://doi.org/10.1351/pac199668122193' target='_blank'>Paper</a>]<br/></div></div>                    </div>
